lector 'matches ZERO lines (found 0)', but the emit-side contract lines (E2:12, E6:12, F1:10) each contain BOTH `OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE` and `[operator-attested]`, and the selector matches on EITHER token. If the cutover flips only the `[non-codebase]` tag while retaining the `OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE:` heading, the line still matches via the heading disjunct, so the count stays 1 and the DIGEST assertion fails rather than the count. The plan never states whether the `OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE` heading is also renamed, nor what token the widened selector should match.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbbc05cb709d4a669","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Why this is ONE commit, gate 1; Acceptance Criteria line 3","norm_id":"n3eb858eb47df4003","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor flips only the tag and keeps the OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE heading: count stays 1, digest test fails (not the count test), so the plan's predicted 'found 0' failure never appears and the widening instruction seems unnecessary","Executor widens the selector to also match `[non-codebase]` but leaves `OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE` in the disjunction: emit-side prompts still count as contract lines, so the count/digest pins must be recomputed to a nonzero count, contradicting the implied 'these files no longer carry the contract' framing"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State whether the emit-side `OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE` heading is retained or renamed, and give the exact widened selector predicate (e.g. add a `\"[non-codebase]\" in ln` disjunct), then reconcile gate 1's 'found 0' claim with the fact that the heading token would otherwise keep the lines matching.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal"